      "explanation": "Sn can exist in +2 or +4 oxidation state. So, Q in the given reactions can be SnCl<sub>2</sub> or SnCl<sub>4</sub>. Since X is monoanion having trigonal pyramidal geometry (sp<sup>3</sup> with one lone pair as per VSEPR), so Q is SnCl<sub>2</sub>, and the first reaction is \n<br> <img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksuss7hs/27d4bbe1-7c1d-4ce6-ac02-b7d38550ee16/f6785f00-0773-11ec-a0ab-05c984536117/file-1ksuss7ht.jpeg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2019 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - p-Block Elements Question 62 English Explanation 1\">\n<br> The second reaction is Stephen’s reaction, where nitrile is converted to aldehyde via formation of iminium salt. \n<br> <br><picture><source media=\"(max-width: 320px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksusu6s2/60314e7b-6110-4422-8c2e-6d9363ded06c/2d898230-0774-11ec-a0ab-05c984536117/file-1ksusu6s3-320w.jpeg\"><source media=\"(max-width: 500px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksusu6s2/60314e7b-6110-4422-8c2e-6d9363ded06c/2d898230-0774-11ec-a0ab-05c984536117/file-1ksusu6s3-500w.jpeg\"><img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksusu6s2/60314e7b-6110-4422-8c2e-6d9363ded06c/2d898230-0774-11ec-a0ab-05c984536117/file-1ksusu6s3.jpeg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2019 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - p-Block Elements Question 62 English Explanation 2\"></picture>\n\n<img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksut5pb3/a912fe0a-944b-4b90-9e72-5d92ace292f7/6dc02600-0775-11ec-a0ab-05c984536117/file-1ksut5pb4.jpeg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2019 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - p-Block Elements Question 62 English Explanation 3\">\n\n<br> There is a coordinate bond in the Cl<sub>2</sub>Sn.N(CH<sub>3</sub>)<sub>3</sub> in between nitrogen and Sn metal.\n<br> <picture><source media=\"(max-width: 320px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksut2z7f/136c693d-80b1-44c7-a936-7081c8e42cf9/21f7f8b0-0775-11ec-a0ab-05c984536117/file-1ksut2z7g-320w.jpeg\"><source media=\"(max-width: 500px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksut2z7f/136c693d-80b1-44c7-a936-7081c8e42cf9/21f7f8b0-0775-11ec-a0ab-05c984536117/file-1ksut2z7g-500w.jpeg\"><img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksut2z7f/136c693d-80b1-44c7-a936-7081c8e42cf9/21f7f8b0-0775-11ec-a0ab-05c984536117/file-1ksut2z7g.jpeg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2019 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - p-Block Elements Question 62 English Explanation 4\"></picture>\n<br> Z is oxidised product and oxidation state of Sn is +4 in Z compound. Structure of SnCl<sub>4</sub> (Z) is\n<br> <img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksut8yjv/340b191a-66d4-4df0-bacb-28bc118e32b5/c8516bb0-0775-11ec-a0ab-05c984536117/file-1ksut8yjw.jpeg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2019 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - p-Block Elements Question 62 English Explanation 5\">"
